    "step": {
      "user": {
        "title": "Connect to Intergas Xtend",
        "description": "## Before you continue\n\nThe Xtend must be reachable over Wi-Fi from this Home Assistant device.\n\n> **Important:** Because the Wi-Fi adapter will be dedicated to the Xtend network, your Home Assistant server must be connected to your home network and internet via **Ethernet**. Without a wired connection, Home Assistant will lose internet access while the Wi-Fi is connected to the Xtend.\n\n**Step 1 — Activate the Xtend access point**\nPress the button on the Xtend unit until the LED blinks purple.\n\n**Step 2 — Connect Home Assistant to the Xtend Wi-Fi**\nGo to [Settings → System → Network](/config/network), click on your Wi-Fi adapter, scan for access points and select **Xtend_xxxxxxxxxx** (WPA-PSK). The password is printed on the Xtend unit.\n\n**Step 3 — Enter the IP address below**\nThe Xtend always uses **10.20.30.1** on its own network. Leave the default unless you have changed it.",
        "data": {
          "host": "IP Address",
          "port": "Port"
        },
        "data_description": {
          "host": "IP address of the Xtend unit (default: 10.20.30.1)",
          "port": "HTTP port of the Xtend unit (default: 80)"
        }
      },
